  "open_questions_the_candidate_answers": [
    "valid_from mixes two formats in one field today ('2026-08-05' and '2026-08-26T17:35:36.000Z'). Both are legal RFC 3339 and they are not the same string, so the same instant has two spellings and two action_ids. Integer Unix seconds removes the class: it is what 8.1 `ts` already uses.",
    "key_type is required so 'was this receipt signed by a key in the registry' is mechanisable — an Ethereum address is a hash of a public key, not a public key.",
    "custody is required per key, which is where the field both sides agreed on belongs: custody is a property of a key, not of every receipt, and it becomes anchored and chained for free."
  ],
